## 5. Data model

Keep prescription and record separate. This was right in `CLAUDE.md` and stays.

### 5.1 Reference data (static, ships with the app)

```
exercise
  exercise_key            PK, slug
  name                    display
  movement_pattern
  muscle_group            rollup for stat attribution
  target_muscle_primary
  target_muscle_secondary
  equipment
  is_compound             bool
  is_unilateral           bool
  coaching_cue

split
  split_id                PK
  name, experience_level, days_per_week, primary_goal
  recommended_schedule, description

workout_day
  workout_id              PK
  split_id                FK
  day_name, day_order, warmup_notes, session_focus

slot                      ← replaces flat exercise instances
  slot_id                 PK
  workout_id              FK
  slot_order
  movement_pattern
  working_sets, rep_range, target_rpe, rest_seconds, tempo
  coaching_cue

slot_option
  slot_id                 FK
  exercise_key            FK
  option_rank             1 = primary, 2 = first alternative, 3 = second
```

The `slot` / `slot_option` split is the structural change. Today a row in `exercises_master` *is* an exercise. In v1 a slot is a movement-pattern requirement with two or three exercises that satisfy it. That's what makes swapping work and it matches the locked design decision about slots.

### 5.2 User data

```
profile
  name, gender, age, height, weight_current, weight_target
  goal, focus_area, fitness_level, activity_level
  training_days_per_week, limitations[]
  created_at

plan
  split_id                which split was selected
  training_weekdays[]     e.g. [Mon, Tue, Thu, Fri]
  start_date
  status                  active | abandoned

scheduled_session
  session_id              PK
  plan_id, workout_id     FK
  date                    real calendar date
  status                  upcoming | completed | missed | rest

logged_set
  session_id, slot_id, exercise_key     FK
  set_index
  weight, reps
  rpe                     optional
  completed_at

session_feedback
  session_id              FK
  difficulty              1–5, single tap at session end
```

`session_feedback` is one tap. It exists because Recovery (§7.4) needs a real input, and a recovery number with nothing behind it is a lie the user will eventually catch.

### 5.3 Swapping

When a user swaps, write the `exercise_key` they actually used onto the `logged_set`. The slot records what was prescribed; the log records what happened. Working weights are tracked per `exercise_key`, so swapping to the dumbbell version doesn't inherit the barbell's loads.

