## 7. The game system

### 7.1 Stats — what they mean

Four stats, each derived from a distinct, real training quality. Nothing is allocated by the user.

| Stat | Represents | Earned from |
|---|---|---|
| **STR** | Maximal force | Completed sets on `is_compound = true` exercises at rep ranges topping out at 8 or below |
| **AGI** | Control and coordination | Completed sets on `is_unilateral = true` exercises, and any set at 12+ reps |
| **VIT** | Work capacity | Total completed sets across all sessions, plus posterior-chain and core slots |
| **INT** | Training discipline | Sessions completed as prescribed: no skipped slots, deloads honored, calibration graduated |

INT is the one that needed defining. It is not trivia knowledge — it's how well you execute the plan. It rises when you finish what was prescribed, including the boring weeks. A user who trains hard but randomly is strong and dumb, and the HUD should say so.

### 7.2 Stat math

Each completed set awards points to one or more stats. Displayed stat value grows sub-linearly so early progress feels fast and later progress feels earned:

```
stat_value = floor( 4 * sqrt(stat_points) ) + baseline_from_questionnaire
```

**Stats never decrease.** The questionnaire sets a baseline floor; logged work only adds. This avoids the "your STR dropped" moment when real data contradicts a self-reported estimate, and it's defensible — you do not get weaker by logging a workout.

### 7.3 XP, levels and tiers

**XP is awarded for adherence, not tonnage.** A completed prescribed set is worth the same XP whether it's a heavy week or a deload week. This deliberately solves the problem where the app punishes you for correctly following its own deload prescription.

```
xp_for_level(n) = round( 80 * n^1.4 )
```

Level 2 at 80 XP, level 10 at roughly 2,000, level 25 at roughly 7,300. Fast early, slow later.

**Tiers** replace any borrowed rank ladder. Six tiers, banded by level, named to match the stoic register:

```
DORMANT      Lv 1–4
AWAKENED     Lv 5–11
FORGED       Lv 12–20
RELENTLESS   Lv 21–32
UNBROKEN     Lv 33–49
SOVEREIGN    Lv 50+
```

A tier change is the biggest moment in the app. It gets a full-screen modal; a level-up gets a smaller one.

### 7.4 Recovery

Derived from three real inputs: days since last session, adherence to prescribed rest days, and the one-tap difficulty rating from `session_feedback`.

**If there's no data yet, show `—`, not a number.** A fabricated readiness score in a health context is the fastest way to lose a user's trust permanently.

The separate "Readiness Score" from the reference mockup is **cut**. It duplicated Recovery and needed data we don't collect. One honest meter beats two, one of which is decorative.

### 7.5 Current versus target stats

The results screen (§9) shows two stat blocks side by side.

- **Current** — baseline computed from fitness level, activity level, training days and goal.
- **Target** — projected value after 12 weeks of full adherence to the selected plan.

Label the target as a projection, in the interface, in plain words. It is a forecast conditional on showing up, not a promise.

