## 8. Questionnaire

One page. One question fills the screen. JavaScript swaps visibility; answers accumulate in memory and save to storage on completion.

**Requirements:**
- A progress indicator — this is a genuine sequence, so numbering is warranted here.
- Back navigation between questions that preserves answers.
- Browser back button should step back one question, not exit the flow. Use `history.pushState` per question.
- Selecting an option on a single-choice question advances automatically after a short beat. Text and number entry needs an explicit continue.
- Validation happens per question, at the point of answering — never a list of errors at the end.

**Questions, in order:**

| # | Question | Type | Drives |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | What should we call you? | Text | Character name throughout the HUD |
| 2 | Gender | Male / Female / Prefer not to say | Calorie display, stat baseline |
| 3 | Age | Number | Calorie display, under-18 flag (§11) |
| 4 | Height | Number, ft/in or cm | Calorie display |
| 5 | Current weight | Number | Calorie display, baseline |
| 6 | Target weight | Number, skippable | Projection framing |
| 7 | Primary goal | Build muscle / Lose fat / Get stronger / General fitness | **Template selection** |
| 8 | Focus area | Chest & arms / Back & shoulders / Legs & glutes / Balanced | Split selection within goal |
| 9 | Fitness level | Never trained / Trained before, returning / Training consistently | Stat baseline, experience gate on splits |
| 10 | Activity level outside the gym | Mostly sitting / Moderately active / On my feet all day | Calorie display, VIT baseline |
| 11 | Anything we should work around? | Multi-select + none: knee, shoulder, lower back, wrist | Exercise filtering |
| 12 | How many days a week can you train? | 3 / 4 / 5 / 6 | **Split selection** |
| 13 | Which days? | Weekday multi-select, count locked to Q12 | Session scheduling |

**Two changes from your list.** Question 11 (limitations) is new — it's cheap, and prescribing barbell squats to someone with a knee problem is the kind of thing that should be preventable at question time. And the day-count selector starts at 3, not 2: the workbook's lowest split is a 3-day full body, so a 2-day option would have nothing to map to.

**Question 8 needs a decision during build.** Focus area has four options but the workbook has seven splits, and goal already selects among them. Either focus area picks between A/B day variants within a split, or it's advisory only and shown back to the user without driving selection. Don't let it silently do nothing.

