## 10. Visual design system

The brief pins this down: deep black, neon cyan, sharp angular panels, system-alert modals, RPG stat bars. Follow it exactly.

### 10.1 Naming and IP

The aesthetic is not protectable and you can take it as far as you want. Character names, specific rank ladders and verbatim system dialogue from an existing property are. **The character is the user** — their name from question 1 appears in the HUD header. Tiers are the original six in §7.3. Write original system copy.

**Stoic quotes must use public-domain translations.** Marcus Aurelius via George Long (1862) and the Long/Higginson Epictetus are safe. Modern translations — Hays, Waterfield and similar — are under copyright. Store the quote pool in `data/quotes.json` with the translator recorded for each entry.

Quotes appear in exactly four places: the results reveal, rest days, session complete, and tier-up. Not scattered.

### 10.2 Tokens

```css
--void:          #04070B;   /* page */
--panel:         #0A1119;   /* cards */
--panel-raised:  #101B26;   /* modals, active states */
--system-cyan:   #3FE9FF;   /* primary accent, glow, active bars */
--system-blue:   #1B7FFF;   /* bar gradients, secondary */
--tier-violet:   #A46BFF;   /* tier-up only — the rarest color in the app */
--text:          #E6F4FA;
--text-dim:      #6F8598;
--vitality:      #4ADE80;   /* recovery meter */
--breach:        #FF4D5E;   /* missed session */
```

Violet appears only on tier-up. A color the user sees three times a year carries more weight than one used for decoration.

### 10.3 Type

- **Display / HUD:** Chakra Petch — angular, squared terminals, built for this register without being the obvious sci-fi default.
- **Body / data:** Inter, with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on every stat readout, weight entry and set counter.

Tabular figures because columns of numbers must align when they change. That's a functional requirement, not a stylistic one — so it applies to numeric readouts only, not to labels.

### 10.4 Geometry

**Zero border-radius anywhere in the app.** Panels use notched corners via `clip-path`:

```css
clip-path: polygon(12px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 12px), calc(100% - 12px) 100%, 0 100%, 0 12px);
```

Borders are 1px `--system-cyan` at 25% opacity, rising to 60% with an outer glow on active or focused elements. Glow comes from `box-shadow`, never from blur filters — blur on a full-screen dark layout is a performance problem on the phones students actually carry.

### 10.5 Stat bars

Segmented, not continuous. Twenty discrete blocks per bar, filled left to right. Segments read as a quantity you can count; a smooth gradient bar reads as decoration.

### 10.6 Quality floor

Responsive to 360px. Visible keyboard focus on every interactive element — the cyan glow doubles as the focus ring. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables the results reveal and shows the final state immediately. Contrast: `--text-dim` on `--panel` must clear 4.5:1, so verify it and lighten if it doesn't.

